Z||000000||Pat||09-23-1999||01:35 AM||||I keep getting the code 44. It's a new sensor.The car is in outstanding running condition, except for this problem. The code is entered a few times and the runs great.<BR>Disconnect the battery to clear this code, and it's starts running slightly rough again.<BR>I tightened the TBI gasket, Checked for vacuum leaks, and checked the ECM #8 & #15 wires. Could the O2 sensor have low voltage output even though it's new? Or could lean exhaust be caused from the splitfires I installed? The splitfires are NOT what they live up to be! Has anyone had this problem?||||reg||8
Z||000001||AL||09-23-1999||01:48 AM||||well let me tell you for some reason splitfires don't work to good with gm cars, i put them in my t/a and it ran like shit.i put rapid fires and it workes good now. by the way my fiero has them too.||||reg||1
Z||000002||JetroGT||09-23-1999||02:18 AM||||How old is your electrical system? As far as coil, wires, cap and rotor/ or coil packs. Also check your fuel filter. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Pat||09-23-1999||03:33 AM||||It's a 84'...coil working...plug wires are new...cap & rotor good and cleaned up and in good condition...and fuel filter was just cleaned and installed. I always keep it perfectly tuned up, since it's my only car and I put on average 100 miles a day for a delivery service. It just bothers me to know that this O2 sensor wants to tell me that there is some maintainance that I have overlooked. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||K9||09-23-1999||09:33 AM||||Just becouse The O2 is new it dosen't mean it works!!!Try it with a different O2!||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||09-23-1999||10:14 AM||||check all thos nasty ground wires on the block as well as the big ones and the thin ones off the battery.<P>One of those nasty litte things is the ground return for the O2 sensor. I had intermitant 45's in cold weather... I found on bunch of the ground was loose. So far I've gotten down around 40 at night and haven't gotten another.||||reg||1
Z||000006||88 Fiero||09-23-1999||10:22 AM||||In regards to the Split Fire Plugs... A buddy of mine have a spark plug tester and tested on of this...Guess what??? Split Fire Plugs really SUCKS!!! they don't produce the sparks that they promise and the arcing of the sparks is very minimal...It really makes me wonder how they stay on business this long...By the way..the friend who got the Split Fire Plugs is on his 85 Fiero Coupe with the 4.3 Vortec engine on it...His car is what we call it the death trap car...He gutted everything in it including the inside door support just to make his car really light and drives it everyday...||||reg||1
Z||000007||mwbackus||09-23-1999||12:59 PM||||Well that makes very little sense to me.  I just dont see how a little less weight is going to matter much when you have a 4.3 strapped to your back! :-)  Hopefully, I will find out how fun these 4.3's are in a Fiero, I recently aquired a complete low mileage turbocharged/intercooled 4.3 for my next little project..hehe  Now I just need to find a low milleage 88 with a bad motor.<P>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000008||Lynx||09-27-1999||04:50 AM||||I have had two o2 sensors go out in 5000 miles on my 85 SC. So they do go out easy. The easy way to see if it is the sensor is to look at the exhaust at idle if black smoke is coming out that means the O2 sensor thinks its lean so its makin the mixture rich as hell. If its not black its not the sensor. Its really runnin lean.||||reg||12
Z||000009||fieroshop||09-28-1999||11:39 PM||||One thing that I see nobody mentioned is that along with the 02 sensor if the throtle postion sensor is bad it will make the 02 sensor read wrong.<BR>George||||reg||1
